Page.Introduction.Name=NE-Accuracy Introduction
Page.Introduction.Content=Do you think XPerfect is still not as strict as you wish?
Page.Introduction.Content=Not Enough Accuracy (NEAcc. or NEA) take every millisecond into calculation, giving you the most precise accuracy of your gameplay!
Page.Introduction.Content=<s>Autoplay only scored approximately 98% NE-Acc. on my PC.</s>
Page.Introduction.Content=
Page.Introduction.Content=<b>This mod does not affect the judgments of ADOFAI! It is just another way of calculating accuracy!</b>
Page.Introduction.Content=
Page.Introduction.Content=<size=150%>Calculation Method</size>
Page.Introduction.Content=
Page.Introduction.Content=Tiles = the total count of tiles, where each mid-spin is counted as only one tile
Page.Introduction.Content=<color=grey>i.e. Tiles = VE + EP + PP + LP + VL + FailMiss - Midspins</color>
Page.Introduction.Content=
Page.Introduction.Content=For each tile, the score of the tile is (consider only the judgment that pushes you forward):
Page.Introduction.Content=• -100 if no fail is on and it is missed
Page.Introduction.Content=• max(100-abs(x), 0) where x is the deviation from the precise timing of the tile, in milliseconds, no matter what the actual judgment is.
Page.Introduction.Content=<color=grey>i.e. The base score for each tile is 100. Every millisecond of deviation from the precise timing costs 1 score, up to 100 scores. If you miss a tile in no fail mode, its score will be -100.</color>
Page.Introduction.Content=
Page.Introduction.Content=Every TooEarly and TooLate costs an extra 50 scores.
Page.Introduction.Content=Every FailOverload costs an extra 100 scores.
Page.Introduction.Content=TotalScores = sum up the scores above (can be negative)
Page.Introduction.Content=
Page.Introduction.Content=NEAccuracy% = TotalScores / Tiles, in percentage

